Arch-liches aren't very effective pets although they're resistant to
almost (?) everything, and the danger is that if they become wild you
may be in trouble unless you're well prepared.  Now that your arch-lich
is peaceful, it will not become wild (ie. untame) unless you anger it,
so you're actually safer.

As you're a valkyrie, the chances of acquiring Stormbringer (a chaotic
artifact) aren't big.  That artifact is evil because it attacks peaceful
monsters without confirmation.  So watch out when chaotic and wielding
that sword...

Scroll of taming may work but it would probably be wasted as arch-liches
have a very high magic resistance roll.  In the worst case it would
still be peaceful. I would leave the pet on the level it is currently.
You can tame only domestic animals (d, c, h) with appropriate food.

